My kids both read really, really well. (The older one started first grade in public schools reading at a minimum 3rd-grade level. the Munchkin was being sent to a 1st-grade reading group before the fall semester was over, and can comfortably read a Magic Tree House book mostly by herself.) I was playing with the Grasshopper when he was 7, after being convinced by Rob Donoghue (of Evil Hat) that it was worth trying.

The big issues in trying to run a game with all three of us will be keeping the Grasshopper from getting bossy, and the Munchkin&#39;s tendency to go straight to meltdown without much in the way of visible upset beforehand. I&#39;m keeping my eyes peeled for a raindy weekend day when they&#39;re with me, so that we can start more or less as soon as we&#39;ve cleaned up from lunch and let it take as long as it takes.

