My son started just after his 6th birthday, closed handed, he&#39;s never been a great reader (certainly not reading above his grade level) but he could memorize what each card did once he asked and I told him, he stuck to playing a few favorite heroes (1s and 2s), but now getting closer to 8 he is trying more variety, often playing two heroes at once and can read most of the cards though he does interpret the effects wrong sometimes usually its becasue he read it too fast. (2 targets 1 damage vs 1 target 2 damage).

He definitatly could not run the game by himself though in a couple more years that could be possible. My next oldest is 5 now and I&#39;m not seeing her being ready in a year, she has desires to play but doesn&#39;t have the patience, things can change in a year though.
